{"name":"Crepe","hex":"#d4bc94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crepe","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat round pancake-like pastry from Lower Brittany, made with wheat.","A soft thin light fabric with a crinkled surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover in crepe.","To crease (paper) in such a way to make it look like crepe paper"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crepe"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crêpe","blocks":[{"text":"A crêpe is a dish made from unleavened batter or dough that is cooked on a frying pan or a griddle. Crêpes are usually one of two varieties: sweet crêpes or savoury crêpes. They are often served with a wide variety of fillings such as cheese, fruit, vegetables, meats, and a variety of spreads. Crêpes can also be flambéed, such as in Crêpes Suzette."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Crepes_dsc07085.jpg/330px-Crepes_dsc07085.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr%C3%AApe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cr%C3%AApe_opened_up.jpg/500px-Cr%C3%AApe_opened_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Cr%C3%AApe_opened_up.jpg/500px-Cr%C3%AApe_opened_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sweet crêpe opened up, with whipped cream and strawberry sauce on it","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACr%C3%AApe_opened_up.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/202412_%E5%BD%A9%E8%99%B9%E5%8D%83%E5%B1%A4%E8%9B%8B%E7%B3%95%E8%88%87%E8%8D%89%E8%8E%93%E5%A5%B6%E6%B2%B9%E5%8D%83%E5%B1%A4%E8%9B%8B%E7%B3%95%28Photo_by_Junyu-K%29.jpg/500px-202412_%E5%BD%A9%E8%99%B9%E5%8D%83%E5%B1%A4%E8%9B%8B%E7%B3%95%E8%88%87%E8%8D%89%E8%8E%93%E5%A5%B6%E6%B2%B9%E5%8D%83%E5%B1%A4%E8%9B